TuxCare offers a portfolio of security solutions for Linux and open-source software aimed at enterprise organizations. With TuxCare, enterprises can automate live vulnerability patching, minimize downtime, keep their applications secure and compliant, and get support from a team that knows Linux security best – covering the most popular Linux distributions, end-of-life systems, programming languages, and much more.
KernelCare, part of TuxCare, delivers enterprise-grade live kernel patching that applies critical security updates and bug fixes to popular Linux kernels without requiring system reboots. This enables organizations to keep their infrastructure secure and up to date while maintaining system availability.
Learn more about TuxCare and KernelCare:
https://tuxcare.com/
https://tuxcare.com/enterprise-live-patching-services/kernelcare-enterprise/
We are looking for experienced Kernel Developers to join the KernelCare Team. This role is ideal for engineers with strong C programming skills, deep knowledge of Linux and Linux kernel development, and an interest in cybersecurity.
As a Kernel Developer, you will work on developing and maintaining Linux kernel patches, with a strong focus on addressing security vulnerabilities and ensuring the stability and reliability of customer systems. You will tackle complex, low-level engineering challenges and contribute directly to solutions that help organizations keep their Linux infrastructure secure without unnecessary downtime.
As a Kernel Developer, your key responsibilities will include:
Ensuring Linux kernels are updated in a timely manner with security fixes and patches addressing known CVEs;
Maintaining and supporting existing kernel functionality while contributing to the development and implementation of new feature;
Contributing to automation efforts when needed by developing Python and Bash scripts, for example, to support CVE patch testing. The primary responsibility for automation remains with a dedicated team.
To be successful in this role, you should have:
Strong proficiency in C programming and exceptional debugging skills;
Experience with Linux kernel core subsystems;
Extensive experience with GDB and other debuggers;
Basic understanding of kernel ABI;
Proficiency in Git for development, patch management, and branch management;
Exceptional problem-solving and strategic thinking skills;
Strong planning, time management, decision-making, presentation, and organizational abilities;
Experience automating routing tasks with AI tools;
Experience with Python and shell scripting;
Ability to thrive in an agile, fast-paced environment;
English Upper-Intermediate (B2) or higher for clear team communication.
Nice to have:
Expertise in CPU performance and power analysis;
In-depth knowledge of CPU and cache architectures;
Basic understanding of x86-64 Assembly (AT&T asm);
Prior exposure to Jenkins.
What's in it for you?
A focus on professional development;
Interesting and challenging projects;
Fully remote work with flexible working hours, which allows you to schedule your day and work from any location worldwide;
Paid 24 days of vacation per year, 10 days of national holidays, and unlimited sick leaves;
Compensation for private medical insurance;
Co-working and gym/sports reimbursement;
Budget for education;
The opportunity to receive a reward for the most innovative idea that the company can patent.
By applying for this position, you consent to the processing of your personal data as described in our Privacy Policy (https://tuxcare.com/privacy-policies-hub/candidate-privacy-notice/), which provides detailed information on how we maintain and handle your data.

Coherent Solutions is a digital product engineering company focused on empowering business success. Our global team of 1700+ talented professionals collaborate seamlessly to deliver innovative solutions that drive measurable business impact. Headquartered in Minneapolis, USA, the company’s core competencies across 10 locations worldwide include product software development, IT consulting, data and analytics, machine learning, mobile app development, DevOps, Salesforce, and more.

We grow a team of advisors, not just order takers, and strive to make the company a place for career growth and opportunities. If you want to grow your core competencies, share your passion and be sure that every contribution is evaluated, we are on the same page.

Company Background
Our client is a global technology company transforming the way brands and agencies make marketing decisions. Its platform enables marketers to plan and activate cross-channel, programmatic media campaigns using real-time research, proprietary audience data, advanced analytics, and more than 150 integrated partners including Facebook, Instagram, Pinterest, Snapchat, and Twitter. The company operates across North America, Europe, the Middle East, Asia, and Australia.

Project Description
The role is focused on developing and modernizing real-time DSP serving services that process bid requests, deliver ads, integrate with third-party platforms, and record measurement events used for reporting and billing. The team works on high-throughput, low-latency systems processing millions of requests per second, with a strong focus on availability, data correctness, performance tuning, and scaling the platform for future growth. Current initiatives include splitting a monolith into microservices, improving deployment automation, and moving measurement pipelines from batch processing to real-time streaming with Kafka.

Technologies
Java
Kafka / Kinesis
Redis
S3
Tomcat
Docker, K8S
Git, CI/CD

What You'll Do
Develop critical high-performance, large-scale services for DSP programmatic integrations and platform products;
Work closely with the Product team to understand business needs and translate product requirements into technical solutions;
Write clean, efficient, and production-ready code with a strong focus on high throughput and low latency;
Design, develop, test, and improve new and existing platform features;
Contribute to building large-scale distributed systems processing billions of transactions per day under strict SLAs;
Improve test coverage, monitoring coverage, automation, and overall system observability;
Follow Agile methodologies and work in a fast-paced engineering environment with quick delivery cycles;

Job Requirements
5+ years of commercial experience in Java backend development, with a focus on scalable backend systems;
Strong knowledge of the JVM ecosystem, including garbage collection, profiling, and performance tuning;
Experience with distributed REST APIs, fault tolerance, scalability, consistency, and resilience;
Hands-on experience with low-latency and high-throughput services;
Experience with real-time streaming pipelines using Kafka, Kinesis, or similar technologies;
Strong knowledge of data structures and algorithms;
Experience with web/application servers such as Tomcat;
Solid understanding of networking and load balancing concepts;
Production experience with Docker and Kubernetes;
Experience with Git and CI/CD pipelines, such as GitLab CI/CD or similar tools;
Interest in applying modern technologies and AI-assisted development tools;
Readiness to participate in PagerDuty rotation (1 week per quarter);
Strong verbal and written communication skills, including the ability to explain complex technical trade-offs to both technical and non-technical stakeholders;
English: B2 or higher;

Nice To Have
Prior experience in the AdTech industry;
Familiarity with Python or Scala;

What Do We Offer
The global benefits package includes:
Technical and non-technical training for professional and personal growth;
Internal conferences and meetups to learn from industry experts;
Support and mentorship from an experienced employee to help you professional grow and development;
Sports activities to promote a healthy lifestyle;
Flexible work options, including remote and hybrid opportunities;
Referral program for bringing in new talent;
Work anniversary program and additional vacation days.

If this opportunity excites you, send us your resume!
Please, note, that we will consider all the applications with due respect, but only shortlisted candidates will be contacted.

Please take you time to see Coherent Solutions Privacy Policy for Job Applicants for details on how we process your personal data: https://www.coherentsolutions.com/privacy-policy-for-job-applicants

